        "provisionalConceptFamily": "tare-and-unit-count",
        "stem": "A shipment containing $2\\times10^2$ empty boxes and a separate load of identical unpacked items has total mass $9.6\\times10^5$ g. Each empty box weighs $8\\times10^2$ g. Each item weighs $4\\times10^1$ g. After removing 15% of the items, the remaining items must be packed into these boxes, each holding at most 90 items. The new shipment must weigh at most $8.4\\times10^5$ g. What is the maximum number of empty boxes that can also be included, beyond those needed to hold all the remaining items? Give your answer in standard form.",
