        "provisionalConceptFamily": "effective-density-and-dilution",
        "stem": "A liquid contains $2.4\\times10^8$ particles per mL. A process removes exactly 40% of these particles. A sample must retain at least $7.2\\times10^{10}$ particles. It is processed in complete containers of $1.6\\times10^2$ mL each, and each container requires an additional 20 mL of particle-free flushing liquid that cannot be counted towards the sample. Find the minimum total volume of sample and flushing liquid used, in litres. Give your answer in standard form.",
